                        "entry_id": "9da40a5c-422f-3e7b-91df-a32c73179257",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fan of the American Christian rock band Skillet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7626a668-0f9e-4d27-a1b2-02926ae5ee6f",
                                "sense_id": "6c76a2e8-ec16-3954-a04a-776eaf477b2e",
                                "text": "With the kick-off of Skillet's 52-city Awake and Alive tour, it is evident that they won't have difficulty find an American following, as Panheads (a moniker for Skillet fans) across the nation are turning up by the hordes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "deff4102-ee78-4373-8469-8c83647ac5a3",
                                "sense_id": "6c76a2e8-ec16-3954-a04a-776eaf477b2e",
                                "text": "This is Skillet doing what Skillet does. If that does it for you, you've probably already got this; if not, it's unlike to win you over to joining the Panheads."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32eb501f-d57c-49aa-8250-bf27330a8c1a",
                                "sense_id": "6c76a2e8-ec16-3954-a04a-776eaf477b2e",
                                "text": "When they talk about crossover bands–those who have strong fan bases in both the secular and Christian worlds–none may be more popular than Skillet and its dedicated \"Panheads.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
